      "text": "Recall that the absolute value (or modulus) of a complex number $z = a + bi$ is given by $$|z| = \\sqrt {a^2+b^2},$$where $i^2 = -1.$\n\nGiven that $|z_1| = \\left|\\frac{1}{2}\\right|$ and $|z_2| = \\left|\\frac{3}{8}\\right|$, we have\n\n\\begin{align*}\n|z_1 + z_2| &= \\sqrt{(x_1 + x_2)^2 + (y_1 + y_2)^2}\\\\\n&\\leq \\sqrt{x_1^2 + y_1^2} + \\sqrt{x_2^2 + y_2^2}\\\\\n&= \\sqrt{|z_1|^2} + \\sqrt{|z_2|^2}\\\\\n&= \\left|\\frac{1}{2}\\right| + \\left|\\frac{3}{8}\\right|\n\\end{align*}\n\nWe want to minimize $|z_1+z_2|,$ so we work towards equality in the constraint above. Specifically, we can minimize the square of the left-hand side of the above equation, since $|x|^2 + |y|^2 = (|x|+|y|)^2 - 2\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}$ and the right-hand side is always nonnegative. We begin by taking the derivative of the left-hand side and setting it equal to zero. The derivative is given by $$2(x_1 + x_2)x_1' + 2(y_1 + y_2)y_1' = 0,$$where we have used the fact that $f(x_1, y_1) = x_1 + x_2$ and $f(x_2, y_2) = y_1 + y_2.$\n\nA quick sketch shows that this equation has a unique solution such that $x_1 = x_2 = \\frac{1}{4}$ and $y_1 = y_2 = \\frac{3}{8}. This is possible is equivalent to setting $|z_1 + z_2| = 1$, giving the maximal possible value of $|z_1 + z_2|$.\n\nSubstituting $z_1$ and $z_2$, we have $$|z_1 + z_2| = \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{4}}.$$\n[asy]\nunitsize(0.5 centimeters);\n\nreal f (real xreal z1 = real(z2 = 0)\nreal i\n\ncomplex z1, z2\ncomplex z2_ri = re(z2)\nreturn abs(re(z1) - re(z2)) + abs(im(z1) - im(z2))\n]\n\nreturn abs(re(z1) - re(x) + im(z1) - im(z2))\n\nreal z1 = re(z1) + im(z1) * i\nreturn sqrt(abs(z1) * abs(z2))\n]\n\n\nWe start by evaluating $\\left|\\frac{1}{2}\\right|$ and $\\left|\\frac{3}{8}\\right|,$ excluding the direction of the unit vectors, meaning that we look at $(\\pm \\frac{1}{2}, 0)$ and $(0, \\pm\\frac{3}{8}).$ In both cases, we can choose $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\frac{3}{8}$ units in each of the positive $x$ or $y$ direction, since their squares are the same when combined. We may choose agree this time, giving $$|z_1 + z_2| = |(\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{3}{8}) + (\\frac{3}{8} - \\frac{3}{8})i| = \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{4}},$$as desired. The answer is \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{4}}",
